# Custom Plugin Rules

Only TwinTack-authored plugins belong in `plugins/`. Third-party plugins are installed via WP admin and documented in `docs/PLUGIN_INVENTORY.md`.

## Consolidation (porting from legacy repo)

- Copy **one** canonical folder per plugin (production-active version)
- Directory names: lowercase, hyphens, no version suffix (e.g. `twintack-grip-manager`)
- Merge features from duplicate legacy folders before deleting extras
- Bump `Version:` in plugin header after consolidation

## Code standards

- Follow WordPress Plugin Handbook: activation/deactivation hooks, namespaced or prefixed functions
- Prefix: `twintack_` or existing plugin prefix — check before adding new functions
- Admin UI: use WP admin styles, nonces, capability checks
- No secrets in source — use `wp-config.php` constants or options API

## WooCommerce integration

- Use WC hooks and CRUD APIs — avoid direct `$wpdb` unless existing pattern requires it
- Test with variable products and custom product types after changes

## Before removing a plugin

1. Confirm inactive on production (`wp plugin list` or admin check)
2. Search theme and other plugins for dependencies
3. Update `docs/PLUGIN_INVENTORY.md` with removal rationale
